摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"OpenCode on DeepSeek Harness — DSH plugin that keeps OpenCode Zen + Go free-tier models working: session affinity, gateway origin headers, and tool-schema fallback.","id":"gh:1398493081","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-opencode-patch","slug":"viztor/dsh-opencode-patch","topics":["cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","llm","opencode","opencode-zen","session-affinity","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"OpenCode on DeepSeek Harness — DSH plugin that keeps OpenCode Zen + Go free-tier models working: ses"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"sion affinity, gateway origin headers, and tool-schema fallback."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"English  ·  简体中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"dsh-opencode-patch\nOpenCode on DeepSeek Harness\nGateway origin headers · Session affinity · Free-tie"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"r tool fallback · Live dual-mode quota meter"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Quick Start ·\nWhat this fixes ·\nInterface ·\nConfiguration ·\nTroubleshooting ·\nChangelog ·\nContributi"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ick Start ·\nWhat this fixes ·\nInterface ·\nConfiguration ·\nTroubleshooting ·\nChangelog ·\nContributing"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"`dsh-opencode-patch` is a DeepSeek Harness host plugin that keeps **OpenCode Zen & Go** models worki"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ng inside DSH. Connect `claude-sonnet-4-5`, `gpt-5.4`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, `m"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"use-spark-1.3-contributor-free`, `qwen3.8-flash` and the rest of the OpenCode catalog without networ"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"k rejections, Cloudflare challenges, entitlement mismatches, or invisible limits."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"**The default state.** Point DSH at OpenCode with no plugin and the models do not work at all — not "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"on one shape, on any of them:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **The request is not recognised as coming from a coding agent.** DSH sends its own `User-Agent`, a"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"nd no `x-opencode-client`, `x-opencode-project` or `x-opencode-session` at all, so the gateway sees "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"an anonymous SDK call and the traffic falls under the abuse rules the vendor documents for clients t"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"hat do not identify themselves. **The free tier is a separate matter and this is not its cause**: wi"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"th every one of those headers restored, a CLI `User-Agent`, a valid session id and the `read`/`bash`"},{"id":"p7s6","text":" tool schemas the fallback injects, a Zen `-free` model still answers `403 FreeTierError` from outsi"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"de OpenCode while a paid model on the same request answers `200`. The ids are still offered — the re"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"fusal names itself, and hiding a row the vendor may serve is the worse failure — and the headers it "},{"id":"p7s9","text":"restores are for the paid routes and the vendor's stated client rules.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## 🔌 What This Fixes"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| Without the patch | With `dsh-opencode-patch` |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| Zen free models fail with `403 Fre"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"eTierError` | **Offered, and refused in the gateway's own words.** The headers and tool fallbacks ar"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"e restored for the paid routes, but they are not this error's cause — measured with all of them in p"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"lace, a Zen `-free` id still answers `403` while a paid model answers `200`, and the refusal comes f"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"rom the service behind the console rather than from anything a request carries. So the ids stay in t"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"he picker and the refusal surfaces as `400 free_tier_restricted` instead of a hidden row |\n| Only on"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"e API shape can be served per route — the rest answer `500` once the basics work | **Per-model routi"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"ng** — each model dispatched to the endpoint its own SDK names, read from the catalog |\n| Session ID"},{"id":"p9s9","text":"s rejected with `400 MissingSessionID` | **Deterministic `ses_…` session hashing** and affinity acro"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"ss turns |\n| Subagents lose conversation context | **Parent session tracking** (`x-opencode-parent-s"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"ession-id`, `x-parent-session-id`) |\n| Auto Review calls fail with `TRANSPORT: Connection error` | *"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"*Fallback session turn capture** preserving turn state across eval calls |\n| Quotas and balances are"},{"id":"p9s13","text":" invisible | **Live dual-mode composer meter** showing Go quota or Zen pay-as-you-go |\n| Zen keys ca"},{"id":"p9s14","text":"use `403 EntitlementError` on Go usage | **Strict credential isolation** keeping Zen keys away from "},{"id":"p9s15","text":"the Go endpoint |\n| Projects share a single `\"global\"` telemetry bucket | **Dynamic workspace attrib"},{"id":"p9s16","text":"ution** resolved from the active `session.header.cwd` |\n| Gateway `/models` returns a truncated, unn"},{"id":"p9s17","text":"amed list | **Catalog enrichment** (`models.opencode.ai`) with display names, context windows and pr"},{"id":"p9s18","text":"ist | **Catalog enrichment** (`models.opencode.ai`) with display names, context windows and prices |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### 3. How a model's protocol is chosen — and why you configure nothing"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Zen's provider-level SDK is `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`. models.dev names a **different** SDK per mo"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"del only when that model needs one, so the presence of `provider.npm` is the signal — and it is what"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" decides the wire protocol. Nothing is matched by hand:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| models.dev `provider.npm` | models | protocol | served from |\n| :-- | --: | :-- | :-- |\n| _(absent"},{"id":"p12s2","text":")_ | 25 | OpenAI Chat Completions | the route you configured |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## 📜 Compatibility & Verification"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**Verified on DeepSeek Harness `0.2.1` — both the `alpha` and `rc` channels (Node 24+)**"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The harness publishes two **channels**, `alpha` and `rc`, and they are parallel tracks rather than a"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" version ordering: semver sorts `0.2.1-rc.2` _above_ `0.2.1-alpha.5`. The plugin targets two lines o"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"n both channels: **`0.2.1`**, whose `rc` builds `dsh@latest` still carries, and the **`0.2.2`** prer"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"eleases on both channels: `alpha` is at `0.2.2-alpha.3`, and `rc` opened the line with `0.2.2-rc.1` "},{"id":"p15s5","text":"(published under the `next` dist-tag; the test install runs `0.2.2-alpha.2`). The `@deepseek-ai/dsh-"},{"id":"p15s6","text":"typert-protocol` peer range says so exactly:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The first clause covers the `0.2.1` line on both channels: its lower bound (`alpha.1`) sorts below e"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"very `rc` of the same line, so rc needs no separate entry. The second is **not** redundant — semver "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"excludes prereleases unless a comparator in the same `major.minor.patch` tuple carries one, so `<0.3"},{"id":"p17s4","text":".0` alone would silently drop every `0.2.2-*` build, alpha and rc alike. Both clauses stop at `0.3.0"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"`, which leaves the next line a separate decision rather than a silent widening."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The optional `@deepseek-ai/cordis` peer follows the typert range. Each line moved the host core: the"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" `0.2.1` builds peer `~4.0.5` (or a `4.0.5` prerelease), the `0.2.2` alphas a `4.0.6` prerelease, an"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"d `0.2.2-rc.1` `~4.1.0`. A fresh install takes the cordis the **newest** admitted typert build peers"},{"id":"p18s4","text":" on, so a cordis peer that misses it fails with `ERESOLVE`; one that misses an older line's cordis f"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"ails beside a host already installed on that line. The peer therefore admits every one of them and s"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"tops at the next tuple:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Surface | Target |\n| :-- | :-- |\n| **Harness line** | **`0.2.1`** and the **`0.2.2`** prereleases,"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" `alpha` and `rc` channels alike (peer: the range above) |\n| **Host core** | `@deepseek-ai/cordis` `"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"4.0.4` up to `4.1.x`, including the `4.0.5` and `4.0.6` prereleases (optional peer: the range above)"},{"id":"p20s4","text":" |\n| **Plugin package** | `dsh-opencode-patch` |\n| **Host profile** | DSH Web profile (`patchReload:"},{"id":"p20s5","text":"age** | `dsh-opencode-patch` |\n| **Host profile** | DSH Web profile (`patchReload: live`) |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
